Unbreak build of llvmpipe with LLVM 7 (mesa 26.2-devel)

Combines three things:

1. A targeted revert of the LLVM-7-relevant parts of
   https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/35374
   ("meson: Require LLVM 8 or newer"):
   - meson floor back to LLVM >= 7
   - GALLIVM_COROUTINES: the llvm-c coroutine passes API only exists from
     LLVM 8, so compute/mesh/task and tessellation are disabled for LLVM 7
     (fragment/vertex/geometry do not use coroutines)
   - lp_bld_passmgr.c HAVE_CORO gating (llvm-c/Transforms/Coroutines.h does
     not exist in LLVM 7)
   - LLVMBuild{GEP2,InBoundsGEP2,Load2,Call2} wrappers for LLVM < 8
   - pre-LLVM-8 saturated add/sub paths (llvm.{s,u}{add,sub}.sat only exist
     from LLVM 8; uses SSE2/AltiVec intrinsics or generic clamping)

2. The previous patch-build-with-LLVM-7.diff, rebased: debug-info C API
   signature differences (LLVMDIBuilderCreateBasicType/CreateCompileUnit),
   LLVMSetCurrentDebugLocation2 (LLVM 9+), LLVMBuildIntCast2 (LLVM 8+),
   float atomics enum values (LLVM 9+/15+).

3. New guards needed for current main:
   - LLVMBuildFreeze wrapper (instruction only exists from LLVM 10;
     passes the value through unchanged)
   - lp_bld_type.h includes gallivm/lp_bld.h again (an upstream include
     cleanup replaced it with llvm-c/Core.h, which would leave the
     wrappers above invisible to most gallivm code); two files that do
     not reach that header include lp_bld.h directly

